<Sheet Background="" DeveloperKey="14" HasParamBitmap="True" Name="Business Areas &amp; Folders" ParamBitmap="" Showpageaxis="True" Title="&amp;Sheet (&amp;File)&#x000d;&#x000a;A list of folders by &apos;Business Area&apos; by type of folder&#x000d;&#x000a;  &#x000d;&#x000a;A Complex Folder can be made up of either Simple, Custom or other Complex Folder Items.&#x000d;&#x000a;A Complex Folder is dependant on these other Folder Items and the joins between Folders.&#x000d;&#x000a;To see what Folders a Complex Folder is based upon, look at the list of Folders in the &apos;Folder Components&apos; field.&#x000d;&#x000a;Component tables display the table names that make up a Folder.  &#x000d;&#x000a;To improve Query Prediction accuracy it is recommended you Analyze a Folders component tables used in queries.&#x000d;&#x000a; &#x000d;&#x000a; Note: &#x000d;&#x000a;Table components item excludes  tables that are used in Custom Folders, using Custom SQL .&#x000d;&#x000a;Complex Folders may be dependant on other Folders just for their join to other Folders, this type of dependency is not displayed in this Worksheet.&#x000d;&#x000a;If the &apos;Date Component Table Last Analysed&apos; is always &apos;Unknown&apos; then it is likely that the version of the database you are using does not provide this information." TitleAlign="Tiled" TitleBackColor="32896" TitleBitmapReference="" TitleDeveloperKey="72" TitleHtml="&lt;table width=&quot;100%&quot; border=0 cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=center&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;Sheet (&amp;File)&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;&lt;b&gt;A list of folders by &apos;Business Area&apos; by type of folder&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;  &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;A Complex Folder can be made up of either Simple, Custom or other Complex Folder Items.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;A Complex Folder is dependant on these other Folder Items and the joins between Folders.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;To see what Folders a Complex Folder is based upon, look at the list of Folders in the &apos;Folder Components&apos; field.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;Component tables display the table names that make up a Folder.  &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;To improve Query Prediction accuracy it is recommended you Analyze a Folders component tables used in queries.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt; Note: &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;Table components item &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;excludes&lt;/b&gt; &lt;/i&gt; tables that are used in Custom Folders, using Custom SQL .&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;Complex Folders may be dependant on other Folders &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;just&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; for their join to other Folders, this type of dependency is not displayed in this Worksheet.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=#808000&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;p align=left&gt;&lt;font size=2 face=&quot;Arial&quot; color=#feffff&gt;If the &apos;Date Component Table Last Analysed&apos; is always &apos;Unknown&apos; then it is likely that the version of the database you are using does not provide this information.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;&lt;/table&gt;&#x000d;&#x000a;" TitleRtf="{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang2057{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f2\fswiss\fprq2 System;}}&#x000d;&#x000a;{\colortbl ;\red254\green255\blue255;}&#x000d;&#x000a;\viewkind4\uc1\pard\qc\cf1\ul\b\i\f0\fs18 &amp;Sheet (&amp;File)&#x000d;&#x000a;\par \pard\ulnone\i0 A list of folders by &apos;Business Area&apos; by type of folder&#x000d;&#x000a;\par \b0   &#x000d;&#x000a;\par A \f1 C\f0 omplex \f1 F\f0 older can be made up of either \f1 S\f0 imple, \f1 C\f0 ustom or other \f1 C\f0 omplex \f1 F\f0 older \f1 I\f0 tems.&#x000d;&#x000a;\par A \f1 C\f0 omplex \f1 F\f0 older is dependant on these other \f1 F\f0 older \f1 I\f0 tems and the joins between \f1 F\f0 olders.&#x000d;&#x000a;\par To see what \f1 F\f0 olders a \f1 C\f0 omplex \f1 F\f0 older is based upon, look at the list of \f1 F\f0 olders in the &apos;Folder Components&apos; field.&#x000d;&#x000a;\par Component tables display the table names that make up a \f1 F\f0 older.  &#x000d;&#x000a;\par To improve Query Prediction accuracy it is recommended you \f1 A\f0 naly\f1 z\f0 e a \f1 F\f0 olders component tables used in queries.&#x000d;&#x000a;\par  &#x000d;&#x000a;\par  Note: &#x000d;&#x000a;\par Table components item \b\i excludes\b0  \i0  tables that are used in Custom Folders, using \f1 C\f0 ustom SQL .&#x000d;&#x000a;\par Complex \f1 F\f0 olders may be dependant on other \f1 F\f0 olders \b\i just\b0\i0  for their join to other \f1 F\f0 olders, this type of dependency is not displayed in this \f1 W\f0 orksheet.&#x000d;&#x000a;\par If the &apos;Date Component Table Last Analy\f1 s\f0 ed&apos; is always &apos;Unknown&apos; then it is likely that the version of the database you are using does not provide this information.\b\f2\fs20 &#x000d;&#x000a;\par }&#x000d;&#x000a;" UniqueName="{5A751724-D200-11D5-B05B-00C04FEDB835}">
